hey everyone what's up this is luca  nigoyda i'm a data scientist and  ecologist and i'm super stoked to be  launching my new course on data  visualization in r for ecologists so  this is the course that i wish i had  as a grad student in ecology if you're  an ecologist or a biologist and want to  quickly learn the essential tools for  making good figures  this course is for you i try to  summarize everything together in  this nice concise three hour short  course that goes over all the basics of  plotting data efficiently and  effectively trying to reduce the r  learning curve as much as possible just  to the essential tools that you need to  really create  professional and publication ready  figures in our  through project based lessons and  exercises i really just take you by the  hand beginning with the most  basics such as how to plot figures using  rs base package  but then moving on to more advanced  topics such as gg plot 2  what it actually is how it works and  beginning to create plots using gg plot  2  specifically focusing on five of the  most essential  and common figures that you find in  ecology and how to plot them how to  customize them how to annotate them  along the way of course we're also going  to cover how to save and export your  figures  and then also some of the best practices  for creating publication quality figures  though this is an introductory course to  data visualization  i do assume that you're going to be  coming into it with just a little bit of  a background in r and r studio  at least the basics knowing how to do  some very basic things with your data  will be important so that i don't  because i'm not going to really spend a  lot of time on  those topics in this course so and it's  just going to go right into data  visualization  if you don't really have that background  if you're still starting from scratch  and don't really know what to do  then definitely check out my other  course on the basics of r for ecologists  which offers a complete foundation in  all the basics that you need to know for  working with data in r  and so if you want to learn more about  that course there's a link down below  or actually maybe it's up above i'm not  really sure where on this website the  links will be  but somewhere on this website where  you're watching this video there will be  links for signing up for  the basics of art for ecologists as well  as this new course on the intro to  data visualization with r for ecologists  thank you so much for watching hope you  enjoyed  please share this with all your friends  with your university with your  department whoever you think might  enjoy these courses or benefit from them  so until then  thanks again and i'll see you there  you
 

